// Guards and compensation, end to end (T5.4, REQ-LANG-14, REQ-AUTO-1, 4).
//
// `booking-compensation.flow` beside this one is the *policy* showcase and is a
// faithful sibling of `execution.flow`. This file is the one that demonstrates
// the two guarantees T5.4 is about, on the smallest thing that can show them:
//
//   * a guard whose predicate is false never performs its step, and the audit
//     log has no surface call for it (REQ-AUTO-1);
//   * a failing story runs its compensating story with the failing story's
//     scope, and the run ends `aborted` with the policy recorded (REQ-AUTO-4).

// ── guards ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// Three guards, one of each subject the IR has: the page, the scope, and the
// step's own element. The two that are false must leave no trace on the
// application at all.

story: I want to see guards decide
  Click the Book a slot link
  Remember the text of the booking status as status
  // True: the page is the booking page.
  Only if the URL contains "/booking", Type "Indiranagar" into the location field
  // False: the status says "Confirmed", so this never runs.
  Only if {status} is "Cancelled", Click the cancel booking button
  // False the other way round: `Unless` runs the step when the predicate fails.
  Unless {status} is "Confirmed", Click the cancel booking button
  // True: the element the step acts on is there.
  Only if the Book now button is visible, Click the Book now button
  The booking result should say "Slot booked."

// ── compensation ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// The booking is made, its reference is remembered, and then a step fails. The
// policy runs "cancel a booking" — which reads `{reference}` out of the failing
// story's scope, because that is the whole point of running it with that scope
// (REQ-AUTO-4) — and the flow stops.

scenario (onFailure=compensate:cancel a booking): I want to book and then fail
  Click the Book a slot link
  Type "Indiranagar" into the location field
  Click the Book now button
  Remember the text of the booking reference as reference
  // There is no such element on the booking page: the step fails with a
  // `locator` class, which is what triggers the policy.
  Click the pay button

scenario (idempotent=true): cancel a booking
  Click the cancel booking button
  // The compensating story can see what the failing one captured. A story that
  // could not would have nothing to cancel.
  The booking reference should say {I want to book and then fail.reference}

test: I want to see guards decide
